{
  "id": "changing-a-pipeline-constructor-default-requires-updating-ma",
  "title": "Changing a Pipeline constructor default requires updating make_pipeline, docstrings, repr/get_params tests and a changelog fragment",
  "kind": "rule",
  "answers": [
    "what else needs updating when I change a Pipeline parameter default",
    "test_pprint fails after changing Pipeline default",
    "get_params expected dict in test_set_pipeline_step_passthrough mismatch"
  ],
  "body": "A Pipeline default appears in several places that this PR had to update together:\n- sklearn/pipeline.py:Pipeline.__init__ and sklearn/pipeline.py:make_pipeline both have the default in their signature and docstring. Add a `.. versionchanged::` entry in each docstring.\n- `_parameter_constraints` must accept the type of the new default. Here a tuple was added for `transform_input`.\n- sklearn/tests/test_pipeline.py:test_set_pipeline_step_passthrough has the full get_params dict hard-coded.\n- sklearn/utils/tests/test_pprint.py has Pipeline's full repr text hard-coded, e.g. `transform_input=('X_val',)`.\n- Add a changelog fragment at doc/whats_new/upcoming_changes/sklearn.pipeline/<PR>.fix.rst.",
  "applies": "Any change to Pipeline/make_pipeline constructor parameters or defaults",
  "tags": [
